ot expire and will be used only if the monthly limit is reached.</p></div><div class="max-w-[1300px] relative mx-auto"><div class="hidden w-[250px] md:flex absolute right-[80%] bottom-[-20px]"><div class=""></div></div><div class="hidden w-[250px] md:flex absolute left-[80%] bottom-[-20px]"><div class=""></div></div><div class="max-w-[510px] xl:max-w-[714px] mx-auto mb-[40px] rounded-[30px] bg-[#FFFFFF60] pt-[118px] px-[16px] pb-[56px] flex flex-col items-center"><div class="w-full max-w-[380px] mx-auto"><div class="relative w-[100%] h-[15px] bg-[#ED800829] mb-[38px] rounded-[50px]"><input type="range" min="1500" max="20000" step="100" class="absolute top-0 left-0 w-full h-full opacity-0 z-10 cursor-pointer " value="5000"/><div style="width:18.91891891891892%" class="absolute top-0 left-0 h-full rounded-[30px] bg-ogGradBottom transition-all"></div><div style="left:18.91891891891892%;transform:translateX(-50%)" class="transition-all w-[23px] h-[23px] flex items-center justify-center rounded-[50px] bg-ogGradBottom absolute top-[-4px] shadow-md"><span class="bg-white w-[15px] h-[15px] shadow-md rounded-[50px]"></span></div><span class="transition-all absolute sahdow-sm bottom-[calc(100%+16px)] text-center text-[16px] leading-[120%] block w-[162px] p-[12px] rounded-[16px] bg-white " style="left:18.91891891891892%;transform:translateX(-18.91891891891892%)">Deep Dive Pages: <br/><span class="text-[24px] block mt-2"> <!-- -->5,000</span></span></div></div><button type="button" class="md:w-[unset] w-[100%] inline-flex justify-center items-start text-[16px] font-semibold py-[16px] px-[22px] md:py-[20px] md:px-[30px] rounded-[43px] border tracking-[-0.02em] transition shadow-lg hover:bg-ogGradBottom hover:text-[#ffffff] active:bg-gradient-to-b active:from-[#E6AC00] active:to-[#E27919] active:shadow-none active:scale-[0.98] active:transform bg-[#242424] text-[#ffffff] border-[#ffffff30] !justify-center !w-[100%] !max-w-[380px] mt-6"><span class="text-[16px] leading-[21.6px] tracking-[-0.02em]">$69 USD</span></button></div></div><div class="text-center"><p class="text-[12px] font-regular md:text-[16px] leading-[135%] text-[#242424] tracking-[-0.02em]">Education discounts available.<a href="mailto:support@socrates.im" class="block text-[#FB9937] hover:text-[#FDAC1C] active:text-[#E88019] font-semibold md:inline-block ml-2">Contact Support.</a></p></div></div></div></section><section class="py-[80px] overflow-hidden md:py-[100px]  xl:py-[120px] bg-[#f4f2ee]"><div class=" "><div class="px-4"><div class="max-w-[710px] mx-auto text-center mb-[40px] md:mb-[50px] xl:mb-[60px]"><div class="w-[44px] h-[44px] md:w-[66px] md:h-[66px] flex mx-auto mb-[20px] md:mb-[30px] shadow-lg rounded-[16px]"><img alt="" loading="lazy" width="68" height="68" decoding="async" data-nimg="1" class="w-[100%]" style="color:transparent" src="/_next/static/media/reviews.6a31d259.svg"/></div><h2 class="text-[28px] font-regular md:text-[52px] leading-[110%] xl:mb-[60px] text-[#242424] text-center xl:text-[60px] tracking-[-0.03em]">Trusted by Professionals</h2></div></div><div class="slick-slider max-w-[1440px] mx-auto px-[2px] mb-[60px] md:mb-[116px] slick-initialized" dir="ltr"><button type="button" data-role="none" class="slick-arrow slick-prev slick-disabled" style="display:block"> <!-- -->Previous</button><div class="slick-list"><div class="slick-track" style="width:173.91304347826087%;left:0%"><div data-index="0" class="slick-slide slick-active slick-current" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="false" style="outline:none;width:25%"><div><div class="mx-[1px] p-[30px] md:p-[52px] bg-white rounded-[30px]  flex flex-col h-[100%]"><p class="mb-[20px] xl:mb-[32px] font-light [&amp;&gt;b]:font-semibold text-[10px] md:text-[14px] xl:text-[18px] leading-[135%] text-black text-opacity-80">Been building some knowledge bases for myself. Tried out several tools like Notebook LM, Afforai and TextCortex. I tested them against each other and<!-- --> <b>Socrates with their deep dive functionality has the most thorough retrieval.</b><br/><br/>This was my test: I uploaded a markdown document with 55 articles with more than 117K words. Each article title preceded by a # sign. Then asked the tools to give me a list of the articles.<br/><br/>The results were:<br/>Afforai returned 12 names.<br/>Notebook LM returned 26 names.<br/><b>Socrates returned 50 names.</b><span class="inline-flex gap-1"><img alt="heart" loading="lazy" width="20" height="20" decoding="async" data-nimg="1" class="motion-safe:animate-[wiggle_2s_ease-in-out_infinite] origin-center" style="color:transparent" src="/images/trusted/heart.svg"/></span></p><div class="flex justify-between items-center mt-auto"><div class="flex items-center"><div class="w-[36px] h-[36px] flex mr-[15px] "><img alt="" loading="lazy" width="50" height="50" decoding="async" data-nimg="1" class="w-[100%] h-[100%] object-cover" style="color:transparent" srcSet="/_next/image?url=%2Fimages%2Ftrusted%2F2.png&amp;w=64&amp;q=75 1x, /_next/image?url=%2Fimages%2Ftrusted%2F2.png&amp;w=128&amp;q=75 2x" src="/_next/image?url=%2Fimages%2Ftrusted%2F2.png&amp;w=128&amp;q=75"/></div><p class="text-[16px] text-[#242424] tracking-[-0.02em] leading-[110%]">EZnl</p></div><div class="flex w-[108px] "><img alt="" loading="lazy" width="128" height="25" decoding="async" data-nimg="1" class="w-[100%]" style="color:transparent" src="/_next/static/media/stars.00204343.svg"/></div></div></div></div></div><div data-index="1" class="slick-slide slick-active" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="false" style="outline:none;width:25%"><div><div class="mx-[1px] p-[30px] md:p-[52px] bg-white rounded-[30px]  flex flex-col h-[100%]"><p class="mb-[20px] xl:mb-[32px] font-light [&amp;&gt;b]:font-semibold text-[10px] md:text-[14px] xl:text-[18px] leading-[135%] text-black text-opacity-80">I recommend Socrates for document analysis. It delivers on its promise to deeply analyze documents at an unmatched level.<br/><br/><b>As a big fan of NotebookLM, I find that Socrates&#x27; Deep Dive feature offers a superior depth of insight.</b> <!-- -->The output from Socrates is impressively accurate and detailed, not the typical verbose responses you might expect from AI tools like ChatGPT.<br/><br/><b>In my opinion, it’s the most precise tool available for analyzing PDFs on the market.<!-- --> <span class="inline-flex gap-1"><img alt="heart" loading="lazy" width="20" height="20" decoding="async" data-nimg="1" class="motion-safe:animate-[wiggle_2s_ease-in-out_infinite] origin-center" style="color:transparent" src="/images/trusted/heart.svg"/></span></b></p><div class="flex justify-between items-center mt-auto"><div class="flex items-center"><div class="w-[36px] h-[36px] flex mr-[15px] "><img alt="" loading="lazy" width="50" height="50" decoding="async" data-nimg="1" class="w-[100%] h-[100%] object-cover" style="color:transparent" srcSet="/_next/image?url=%2Fimages%2Ftrusted%2F2.png&amp;w=64&amp;q=75 1x, /_next/image?url=%2Fimages%2Ftrusted%2F2.png&amp;w=128&amp;q=75 2x" src="/_next/image?url=%2Fimages%2Ftrusted%2F2.png&amp;w=128&amp;q=75"/></div><p class="text-[16px] text-[#242424] tracking-[-0.02em] leading-[110%]">TC_</p></div><div class="flex w-[108px] "><img alt="" loading="lazy" width="128" height="25" decoding="async" data-nimg="1" class="w-[100%]" style="color:transparent" src="/_next/static/media/stars.00204343.svg"/></div></div></div></div></div><div data-index="2" class="slick-slide slick-active" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="false" style="outline:none;width:25%"><div><div class="mx-[1px] p-[30px] md:p-[52px] bg-white rounded-[30px]  flex flex-col h-[100%]"><p class="mb-[20px] xl:mb-[32px] font-light [&amp;&gt;b]:font-semibold text-[10px] md:text-[14px] xl:text-[18px] leading-[135%] text-black text-opacity-80">No more Lazy AIs! (Afforai/NotebookLM+ on steroids)<br/><br/>But immense potential.<!-- --> <b>It gives more in depth analysis of texts than Google&#x27;s NoteBookLM, Afforai, among other &quot;Chat with your PDF&quot; softwares through their DeepDive algorithm<!-- --> <span class="inline-flex gap-1"><img alt="heart" loading="lazy" width="20" height="20" decoding="async" data-nimg="1" class="motion-safe:animate-[wiggle_2s_ease-in-out_infinite] origin-center" style="color:transparent" src="/images/trusted/heart.svg"/></span></b> <!-- -->(AKA: AI on steroids)!<br/><br/>Vs. AfforAI - Socrates&#x27; interface is much quicker.<br/>Vs. NoteBookLM - though it does not have actionable buttons with AI prompts (this would be very cool) nor its podcast feature, it gives more indepth analysis if prompted correctly.<br/>Vs. OpenAI GPT4o or Anthropics 3.5 Sonnet - they often give &quot;lazy answers&quot;.<br/><br/>It is comparable with o1-preview&#x27;s answers.</p><div class="flex justify-between items-center mt-auto"><div class="flex items-center"><div class="w-[36px] h-[36px] flex mr-[15px] "><img alt="" loading="lazy" width="50" height="50" decoding="async" data-nimg="1" class="w-[100%] h-[100%] object-cover" style="color:transparent" srcSet="/_next/image?url=%2Fimages%2Ftrusted%2F2.png&amp;w=64&amp;q=75 1x, /_next/image?url=%2Fimages%2Ftrusted%2F2.png&amp;w=128&amp;q=75 2x" src="/_next/image?url=%2Fimages%2Ftrusted%2F2.png&amp;w=128&amp;q=75"/></div><p class="text-[16px] text-[#242424] tracking-[-0.02em] leading-[110%]">JPark</p></div><div class="flex w-[108px] "><img alt="" loading="lazy" width="128" height="25" decoding="async" data-nimg="1" class="w-[100%]" style="color:transparent" src="/_next/static/media/stars.00204343.svg"/></div></div></div></div></div><div data-index="3" class="slick-slide" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true" style="outline:none;width:25%"><div><div class="mx-[1px] p-[30px] md:p-[52px] bg-white rounded-[30px]  flex flex-col h-[100%]"><p class="mb-[20px] xl:mb-[32px] font-light [&amp;&gt;b]:font-semibold text-[10px] md:text-[14px] xl:text-[18px] leading-[135%] text-black text-opacity-80"><b>I love Socrates.<!-- --> <span class="inline-flex gap-1 mr-1"><img alt="heart" loading="lazy" width="20" height="20" decoding="async" data-nimg="1" class="motion-safe:animate-[wiggle_2s_ease-in-out_infinite] origin-center" style="color:transparent" src="/images/trusted/heart.svg"/></span>The Deep Dive feature is super useful.</b> <!-- -->If you have used Afforai for a while, it is similar to the File Wizard feature that they deprecated. It allows you to apply a prompt to every paragraph, section, or page or a document, and it allows very deep querying of the document. The regular mode interaction with one or more document is also very good. While Afforai is evolving into a different kind of tool, which is great, Socrates is proving to be very good at what it does, making research and understanding complex documents easier. For people who already use Afforai, I recommend still getting this deal for Socrates. They each have different strengths. This is a great deal. If you miss Afforai&#x27;s File Wizard, you are going to love this even more advanced version of it in Deep Dive.</p><div class="flex justify-between items-center mt-auto"><div class="flex items-center"><div class="w-[36px] h-[36px] flex mr-[15px] "><img alt="" loading="lazy" width="50" height="50" decoding="async" data-nimg="1" class="w-[100%] h-[100%] object-cover" style="color:transparent" srcSet="/_next/image?url=%2Fimages%2Ftrusted%2F2.png&amp;w=64&amp;q=75 1x, /_next/image?url=%2Fimages%2Ftrusted%2F2.png&amp;w=128&amp;q=75 2x" src="/_next/image?url=%2Fimages%2Ftrusted%2F2.png&amp;w=128&amp;q=75"/></div><p class="text-[16px] text-[#242424] tracking-[-0.02em] leading-[110%]">drleeds</p></div><div class="flex w-[108px] "><img alt="" loading="lazy" width="128" height="25" decoding="async" data-nimg="1" class="w-[100%]" style="color:transparent" src="/_next/static/media/stars.00204343.svg"/></div></div></div></div></div></div></div><button type="button" data-role="none" class="slick-arrow slick-next" style="display:block"> <!-- -->Next</button></div></div></section><section id="faq" class="py-[60px] md:py-[80px] xl:pb-[200px] xl:pt-[120px] bg-[#f4f2ee]"><div class=" "><div class=" text-center mb-[30px] md:mb-[60px]"><div class="w-[44px] h-[44px] md:w-[66px] md:h-[66px] flex mx-auto mb-[20px] md:mb-[30px] shadow-lg rounded-[16px]"><img alt="" loading="lazy" width="68" height="68" decoding="async" data-nimg="1" class="w-[100%]" style="color:transparent" src="/_next/static/media/faq.a55298ab.svg"/></div><h2 class="text-[28px] font-regular md:text-[52px] leading-[110%] xl:mb-[60px] text-[#242424] text-center xl:text-[60px] tracking-[-0.03em]">Frequently Asked Questions</h2></div><div class="max-w-[1440px] mx-auto flex flex-wrap px-[1px]"><div class="w-[calc(100%-2px)] md:w-[calc(50%-2px)] xl:w-[calc(33.3%-2px)] m-[1px] p-[30px] md:p-[52px] bg-white rounded-[40px] flex flex-col"><h5 class="text-[16px] md:text-[24px] text-[#242424] mb-[16px] font-medium leading-[130%]">Is this free?</h5><p class="text-[16px] md:text-[18px] md:leading-[135%] font-light text-[#7E7C78] tracking-[-0.02em] leading-[110%]">Yes, there is a free plan that lets you play with all of the features of the product. Using Local models like Meta Llama is completely free.</p></div><div class="w-[calc(100%-2px)] md:w-[calc(50%-2px)] xl:w-[calc(33.3%-2px)] m-[1px] p-[30px] md:p-[52px] bg-white rounded-[40px] flex flex-col"><h5 class="text-[16px] md:text-[24px] text-[#242424] mb-[16px] font-medium leading-[130%]">How is Socrates different from other document analysis tools?</h5><p class="text-[16px] md:text-[18px] md:leading-[135%] font-light text-[#7E7C78] tracking-[-0.02em] leading-[110%]">Socrates processes your files in multiple ways, with each pass generating additional memories from which Socrates AI can draw insights. You can learn more<!-- --> <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="text-[#FB9937] hover:text-[#FDAC1C] active:text-[#E88019]" href="https://roadmap.socrates.im/t/help-center#16414-deep-dive-other-advanced-tools">here</a>.</p></div><div class="w-[calc(100%-2px)] md:w-[calc(50%-2px)] xl:w-[calc(33.3%-2px)] m-[1px] p-[30px] md:p-[52px] bg-white rounded-[40px] flex flex-col"><h5 class="text-[16px] md:text-[24px] text-[#242424] mb-[16px] font-medium leading-[130%]">How many languages does Socrates support?</h5><p class="text-[16px] md:text-[18px] md:leading-[135%] font-light text-[#7E7C78] tracking-[-0.02em] leading-[110%]">Socrates supports over<!-- --> <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="text-[#FB9937] hover:text-[#FDAC1C] active:text-[#E88019]" href="https://roadmap.socrates.im/p/set-language-preference-oF6HoY">60 languages.</a></p></div><div class="w-[calc(100%-2px)] md:w-[calc(50%-2px)] xl:w-[calc(33.3%-2px)] m-[1px] p-[30px] md:p-[52px] bg-white rounded-[40px] flex flex-col"><h5 class="text-[16px] md:text-[24px] text-[#242424] mb-[16px] font-medium leading-[130%]">Are my documents kept private and secure?</h5><p class="text-[16px] md:text-[18px] md:leading-[135%] font-light text-[#7E7C78] tracking-[-0.02em] leading-[110%]">Your documents stay local on Mac or Windows apps, with options to use local LLMs like Llama 3 or send encrypted data to Microsoft Azure OpenAI. Microsoft doesn’t train on this data per their data processing agreement. <br/> <br/>Learn more about our<!-- --> <a class="text-[#FB9937] hover:text-[#FDAC1C] active:text-[#E88019]" href="/ai-privacy">Socrates&#x27; AI Data Privacy Guide</a> <!-- -->or Microsoft&#x27;s<!-- --> <a href="https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/legal/cognitive-services/openai/data-privacy" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="text-[#FB9937] hover:text-[#FDAC1C] active:text-[#E88019]">Azure OpenAI Data Privacy</a> <!-- -->policy.</p></div><div class="w-[calc(100%-2px)] md:w-[calc(50%-2px)] xl:w-[calc(33.3%-2px)] m-[1px] p-[30px] md:p-[52px] bg-white rounded-[40px] flex flex-col"><h5 class="text-[16px] md:text-[24px] text-[#242424] mb-[16px] font-medium leading-[130%]">I use Windows. How can I speed up the local LLM?</h5><p class="text-[16px] md:text-[18px] md:leading-[135%] font-light text-[#7E7C78] tracking-[-0.02em] leading-[110%]">If you have an nVidia GPU, you can install<!-- --> <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="text-[#FB9937] hover:text-[#FDAC1C] active:text-[#E88019]" href="https://developer.nvidia.com/cuda-downloads">CUDA</a>, which will provide the speediest local LLM experience. If you have any other GPU, Socrates automatically uses your GPU to speed up the local LLM using Vulkan.</p></div><div class="w-[calc(100%-2px)] md:w-[calc(50%-2px)] xl:w-[calc(33.3%-2px)] m-[1px] p-[30px] md:p-[52px] bg-white rounded-[40px] flex flex-col"><h5 class="text-[16px] md:text-[24px] text-[#242424] mb-[16px] font-medium leading-[130%]">What is the maximum file and chat size?</h5><p class="text-[16px] md:text-[18px] md:leading-[135%] font-light text-[#7E7C78] tracking-[-0.02em] leading-[110%]">Chats can be trained on an unlimited number of files. For cloud chats, each individual file has a max of 10 million characters or max of 150 MB. Each cloud chat supports a max of 100 million characters. <br/><br/> For local chats, there is no size restriction other than your computer&#x27;s storage.</p></div></div><div class="text-center text-[16px] md:text-[20px] px-[20px] pt-[30px] md:pt-[60px]"><p class=" text-[#242424] font-light tracking-[-0.02em] leading-[135%]">Can’t find the answer you’re looking for? Reach out to our<!-- --> <a href="mailto:support@socrates.im" class="text-[#FB9937] hover:text-[#FDAC1C] active:text-[#E88019] font-semibold md:block">customer support team.</a></p></div></div></section><section class="max-w-[1440px] mx-auto px-[40px] py-[100px] xl:py-[120px]  rounded-[40px] bg-[#242424] overflow-hidden relative"><div class="absolute top-0 left-[0] flex w-[415px] md:w-[648px] xl:w-[894px] -translate-x-[50%] md:-translate-x-[56%] md:-translate-y-[15%] xl:-translate-x-[36%] xl:-translate-y-[19%]"><img alt="" loading="lazy" width="974" height="997" decoding="async" data-nimg="1" class="w-[100%]" style="color:transparent" src="/_next/static/media/shape-1.29cdd3c5.svg"/></div><div class="absolute bottom-0 right-[0] rotate-[15deg] flex w-[433px] md:w-[648px] xl:w-[894px] translate-x-[58%] translate-y-[20%] md:translate-x-[56%] md:translate-y-[32%] xl:translate-x-[36%] xl:translate-y-[30%]"><img alt="" loading="lazy" width="974" height="997" decoding="async" data-nimg="1" class="w-[100%]" style="color:transparent" src="/_next/static/media/shape-2.54d28841.svg"/></div><div class="flex flex-col items-center relative z-3"><div class="text-center mb-[60px]"><div class="w-[50px] h-[50px] md:w-[70px] md:h-[70px] flex mx-auto mb-[20px] md:mb-[30px]"><img alt="" loading="lazy" width="51" height="51" decoding="async" data-nimg="1" class="w-[100%]" style="color:transparent" src="/_next/static/media/logo-icon.10214e31.svg"/></div><h2 class="text-[28px] font-regular md:text-[52px] leading-[110%] text-[#ffffff] text-center xl:text-[60px] tracking-[-0.03em] mb-[12px] md:mb-[20px]">Know. Quickly.</h2><p class="text-[16px] md:text-[20px] leading-[110%] opacity-[0.8] text-[#ffffff] tracking-[-0.02em]">Start using our free app today.</p></div><div class="w-[100%] max-w-[285px] md:max-w-[620px]"><div class="flex flex-col md:flex-row max-w-[285px] md:max-w-[620px] mx-auto mb-[30px] justify-center"><a href="https://go.socrates.im"><button type="button" class="md:w-[unset] w-[100%] inline-flex justify-center items-start text-[16px] font-semibold py-[16px] px-[22px] md:py-[20px] md:px-[30px] rounded-[43px] border tracking-[-0.02em] transition bg-transparent shadow-[unset] border-solid border-[1px] hover:bg-transparent hover:border-[#FB9937] active:bg-transparent active:border-[#E88019] border-[#ffffff] text-[#ffffff]"><span class="flex w-[24px] h-[20px] [&amp;&gt;svg]:w-[100%] [&amp;&gt;svg]:h-[100%] mr-[10px] md:mr-[16px] items-center justify-center"><svg viewBox="0 0 25 24" fill="none"><path d="M12.5 22C18.0228 22 22.5 17.5228 22.5 12C22.5 6.47715 18.0228 2 12.5 2C6.97715 2 2.5 6.47715